<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan de Betanzos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1510–<a href="/years/1576">1576</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan de Betanzos was a Spanish chronicler and interpreter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quechua">Quechua</a> in early colonial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>. Married to Cuxirimay Ocllo, a noblewoman of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atahualpa">Atahualpa</a>'s family, he drew on the memories of her relatives for his Suma y narración de los <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Incas</a>, completed in 1551, one of the earliest and most valuable accounts of Inca history.</p></div>
